  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1250 AM Wednesday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Dry weather, with seasonal to below normal\ntemperatures over the next week. \n\nHigh pressure will dominate over the next week. A stronger high \npressure system will reinforce cooler temperatures late week through \nthe weekend. Temperature-wise this will look like highs in the upper \n60s to lower 70s today and tomorrow, before dropping generally into \nthe 60s Friday through the weekend. Low temperatures are likely to \nbe mainly in the upper 30s and 40s through the period. Temperatures \nmay get down into the mid 30s in typical cooler spots Saturday and \nSunday mornings which could allow for patchy frost.  \n\nNo rain is expected through the period, with the next very low \nchance of rain coming from an expected weak and dry cold front\nmid next week.",
